# Test the API from VS Code.
# 1. Install the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao).
# 2. Start the API:  dotnet run --project api
# 3. Click "Send Request" above any request below.
# Requests are separated by ###.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5041/api/applications

### List all applications
GET {{baseUrl}}

### Create an application
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company": "Acme Insurance",
  "role": "Software Engineering Intern",
  "status": "Applied",
  "dateApplied": "2026-09-20",
  "deadline": "2026-10-15",
  "followUpDate": "2026-09-27",
  "notes": "Met the recruiter at the career fair."
}

### Get one application by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/1

### Update an application (PUT sends the full object)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company": "Acme Insurance",
  "role": "Software Engineering Intern",
  "status": "Interviewing",
  "dateApplied": "2026-09-20",
  "deadline": "2026-10-15",
  "followUpDate": "2026-10-01",
  "notes": "Phone screen scheduled."
}

### Delete an application
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/1

### Validation check: missing Company -> expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "Intern",
  "status": "Saved"
}

### Not found check -> expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/9999

### ----- Contacts (nested under an application) -----

### List contacts for application 1
GET http://localhost:5041/api/applications/1/contacts

### Add a contact to application 1
POST http://localhost:5041/api/applications/1/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jordan Lee",
  "title": "Campus Recruiter",
  "email": "jordan.lee@example.com",
  "linkedIn": "linkedin.com/in/jordanlee",
  "notes": "Met at the career fair booth."
}

### Get one contact
GET http://localhost:5041/api/contacts/1

### Delete a contact
DELETE http://localhost:5041/api/contacts/1
